1
00:00:06,470 --> 00:00:12,460
2 basketball players record their points in their last 5 games.

2
00:00:12,510 --> 00:00:15,620
Ana scores 12, 15, 11, 14 and 13.

3
00:00:15,670 --> 00:00:18,960
Bo scores 4, 25, 9, 22 and 5.

4
00:00:19,010 --> 00:00:21,120
What is the mean of Ana's points?

5
00:00:21,170 --> 00:00:24,610
Pause the video and work it out.

6
00:00:24,660 --> 00:00:27,320
Add Ana's points: the total is 65.

7
00:00:27,370 --> 00:00:28,760
Divide by 5 games.

8
00:00:28,810 --> 00:00:31,060
Her mean is 13 points.

9
00:00:31,110 --> 00:00:31,580
Now Bo.

10
00:00:31,630 --> 00:00:34,870
His total is also 65, so his mean is 13 too.

11
00:00:34,920 --> 00:00:37,630
But the 2 players are very different.

12
00:00:37,680 --> 00:00:41,390
We need more than the mean to compare them.

13
00:00:41,440 --> 00:00:46,580
Remember: it helps to write data in order, smallest first.

14
00:00:46,630 --> 00:00:50,600
Ana's points in order are 11, 12, 13, 14, 15.

15
00:00:50,650 --> 00:00:53,390
Bo's are 4, 5, 9, 22, 25.

16
00:00:53,440 --> 00:00:55,380
There are 3 kinds of average.

17
00:00:55,430 --> 00:00:57,720
The mode is the most common value.

18
00:00:57,770 --> 00:01:01,980
Ana and Bo have no mode, because no score is repeated.

19
00:01:02,030 --> 00:01:06,160
The median is the middle value, when the data is in order.

20
00:01:06,210 --> 00:01:07,520
Ana's median is 13.

21
00:01:07,570 --> 00:01:09,300
Bo's median is 9.

22
00:01:09,350 --> 00:01:13,310
The mean is the total, divided by the number of values.

23
00:01:13,360 --> 00:01:15,170
Both means are 13.

24
00:01:15,220 --> 00:01:15,940
Your turn.

25
00:01:15,990 --> 00:01:18,330
Find the mean of 4, 8, 6 and 2.

26
00:01:18,380 --> 00:01:21,810
Pause the video and try it.

27
00:01:21,860 --> 00:01:23,170
The total is 20.

28
00:01:23,220 --> 00:01:24,790
There are 4 values.

29
00:01:24,840 --> 00:01:26,590
20 divided by 4 is 5.

30
00:01:26,640 --> 00:01:28,330
The mean is 5.

31
00:01:28,380 --> 00:01:31,500
The range tells you how spread out the data is.

32
00:01:31,550 --> 00:01:35,420
It is the largest value, minus the smallest value.

33
00:01:35,470 --> 00:01:38,930
Ana's range is 15 minus 11, which is 4.

34
00:01:38,980 --> 00:01:42,900
Bo's range is 25 minus 4, which is 21.

35
00:01:42,950 --> 00:01:46,500
Ana's scores are close together, so she is consistent.

36
00:01:46,550 --> 00:01:49,980
Bo has some great games, and some poor ones.

37
00:01:50,030 --> 00:01:53,990
With an even number of values, there are 2 middle values.

38
00:01:54,040 --> 00:01:57,000
The median is halfway between them.

39
00:01:57,050 --> 00:02:00,930
Find the median of 9, 2, 14, 7, 11 and 4.

40
00:02:00,980 --> 00:02:03,710
In order: 2, 4, 7, 9, 11, 14.

41
00:02:03,760 --> 00:02:07,130
The middle values are 7 and 9.

42
00:02:07,180 --> 00:02:09,570
Halfway between 7 and 9 is 8.

43
00:02:09,620 --> 00:02:11,460
The median is 8.

44
00:02:11,510 --> 00:02:12,230
Your turn.

45
00:02:12,280 --> 00:02:14,750
Find the median of 3, 9, 4 and 7.

46
00:02:14,800 --> 00:02:18,220
Pause the video and try it.

47
00:02:18,270 --> 00:02:20,000
In order: 3, 4, 7, 9.

48
00:02:20,050 --> 00:02:22,550
The middle values are 4 and 7.

49
00:02:22,600 --> 00:02:25,480
Halfway between them is 5.5.

50
00:02:25,530 --> 00:02:26,820
Here is the method.

51
00:02:26,870 --> 00:02:29,960
Step 1: find an average for each set.

52
00:02:30,010 --> 00:02:33,180
Step 2: find the range for each set.

53
00:02:33,230 --> 00:02:34,350
Step 3: compare.

54
00:02:34,400 --> 00:02:36,090
Which average is higher?

55
00:02:36,140 --> 00:02:38,320
Which range is smaller?

56
00:02:38,370 --> 00:02:42,830
Step 4: write 2 sentences, about the real situation.

57
00:02:42,880 --> 00:02:47,680
7 students give their shoe sizes: 3, 5, 5, 6, 5, 8 and 3.

58
00:02:47,730 --> 00:02:49,420
Find the mode.

59
00:02:49,470 --> 00:02:51,150
Size 5 appears 3 times.

60
00:02:51,200 --> 00:02:53,630
That is more than any other size.

61
00:02:53,680 --> 00:02:55,450
So the mode is 5.

62
00:02:55,500 --> 00:02:57,760
2 classes take the same test.

63
00:02:57,810 --> 00:03:01,170
Class A has a mean of 68 and a range of 12.

64
00:03:01,220 --> 00:03:04,580
Class B has a mean of 61 and a range of 30.

65
00:03:04,630 --> 00:03:06,160
Compare them.

66
00:03:06,210 --> 00:03:08,050
Class A has the higher mean.

67
00:03:08,100 --> 00:03:11,090
So on average, Class A scored higher.

68
00:03:11,140 --> 00:03:13,480
Class A also has the smaller range.

69
00:03:13,530 --> 00:03:16,410
So its scores were more consistent.

70
00:03:16,460 --> 00:03:19,210
5 people work at a small company.

71
00:03:19,260 --> 00:03:24,990
Their salaries, in thousands of dollars, are 18, 20, 21, 23 and 168.

72
00:03:25,040 --> 00:03:28,680
Which average shows a typical salary?

73
00:03:28,730 --> 00:03:31,540
The total is 250, so the mean is 50.

74
00:03:31,590 --> 00:03:35,130
But that is more than 4 of the 5 people earn.

75
00:03:35,180 --> 00:03:38,230
1 huge salary pulls the mean up.

76
00:03:38,280 --> 00:03:40,750
The median is the middle value: 21.

77
00:03:40,800 --> 00:03:44,890
That is a much better picture of a typical salary.

78
00:03:44,940 --> 00:03:47,680
Find the median of 8, 3, 6, 1 and 5.

79
00:03:47,730 --> 00:03:49,390
Here is Tom's working.

80
00:03:49,440 --> 00:03:52,110
Which line goes wrong first?

81
00:03:52,160 --> 00:03:53,230
Line 1 is wrong.

82
00:03:53,280 --> 00:03:56,380
You must put the data in order first.

83
00:03:56,430 --> 00:03:58,430
In order: 1, 3, 5, 6, 8.

84
00:03:58,480 --> 00:04:00,320
The middle value is 5.

85
00:04:00,370 --> 00:04:02,240
The median is 5.

86
00:04:02,290 --> 00:04:03,960
A shoe shop uses the mode.

87
00:04:04,010 --> 00:04:09,960
It needs to know which size sells the most, so that it can order more of that size.

88
00:04:10,010 --> 00:04:14,100
News reports often give the median house price, not the mean.

89
00:04:14,150 --> 00:04:18,100
A few very expensive houses would pull the mean up.

90
00:04:18,150 --> 00:04:21,210
And a mean does not have to be a real value.

91
00:04:21,260 --> 00:04:27,490
A country can have a mean of 2.4 people in each home, but no home has 2.4 people.

92
00:04:27,540 --> 00:04:28,750
One last question.

93
00:04:28,800 --> 00:04:32,980
Does a smaller range mean more consistent, or higher scores?

94
00:04:33,030 --> 00:04:36,280
Pause the video and answer.

95
00:04:36,330 --> 00:04:37,380
More consistent.

96
00:04:37,430 --> 00:04:40,840
A small range means the values are close together.

97
00:04:40,890 --> 00:04:44,080
It does not tell you how high they are.

98
00:04:44,130 --> 00:04:47,250
To remember: the mode is the most common value.

99
00:04:47,300 --> 00:04:50,020
The median is the middle value, in order.

100
00:04:50,070 --> 00:04:54,280
The mean is the total, divided by the number of values.

101
00:04:54,330 --> 00:04:57,270
The range is the largest minus the smallest.

102
00:04:57,320 --> 00:04:59,180
It shows the spread.

103
00:04:59,230 --> 00:05:03,890
Compare 2 sets of data with an average, and with the range.

104
00:05:03,940 --> 00:05:07,840
Choose the median when there are extreme values.

105
00:05:07,890 --> 00:05:13,190
Great work! Now practise lesson 16.6 on Camday.
